    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass, including `Cp22Tests`. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for owner creation. The value appears in both the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) responses, so it's a persisted per-owner snapshot computed at creation time \u2014 consistent with the existing derived-and-stored fields like `namesakeCount` and `customerCode`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, reused the daily accumulation count (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`, the same path the daily-limit rule uses) and set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersRegisteredToday > 80)`. Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant. Since owners registered on a day are capped at 100, the warning fires for creates 82\u2013100 on a given day, and is `false` otherwise.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name, so `getOwner` returns the stored value.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the hsqldb profile.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` (fresh create \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` is `false`) passes, and all 32 pre-existing tests remain green.",
